    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.spectral_bipartivity - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.spectral_bipartivity.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.spectral_bipartivity()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Measure how close an undirected graph is to being bipartite (spectral\n    bipartivity).\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.spectral_bipartivity()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Measure how close an undirected graph is to being bipartite (spectral\n    bipartivity).\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.spectral_bipartivity()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Measure how close an undirected graph is to being bipartite (spectral\n  bipartivity).\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nMeasure how close an undirected graph is to being bipartite (spectral bipartivity).\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L24699-L24811){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.spectral_bipartivity(\n    nodes=None,\n    weighted=None,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Spectral bipartivity](../assets/graphs/spectral-bipartivity.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Left: the square 1, 2, 3, 4 has only even cycles, so every closed walk has even length and spectral_bipartivity() returns 1.0. Right: the same square plus the diagonal 1 to 3, in the accent color, which closes the triangles 1, 2, 3 and 1, 3, 4; odd closed walks now count against it and the value drops to 0.795.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nEstrada and Rodríguez-Velázquez (2005) weigh every closed walk by $1 / k!$ for its length\n$k$: a graph is bipartite exactly when it has no closed walks of odd length, so the share\nof even closed walks, $\\mathrm{tr}\\cosh(A) / \\mathrm{tr}\\, e^{A}$, equals 1 for bipartite\ngraphs and drops toward 1/2 as odd cycles (triangles above all) take over. It grades\n\"almost bipartite\" networks, such as protein interaction or food webs with a two-mode\nbackbone. Per-node values show which nodes take part in odd cycles.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[nodes]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [list[Union[int, str]] | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional nodes (IDs or labels): return each node's own bipartivity,\n    $\\cosh(A)_{ii} / (e^A)_{ii}$, instead of the graph value.\n\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether to use edge weights in $A$. If `None` (default), follows the graph's\n    `weighted` flag.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [float or dict[int, float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The graph's bipartivity (between 1/2 and 1), or a node-to-value dictionary.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is directed or a node does not exist.\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nThe matrix functions are evaluated from one symmetric eigendecomposition\n$A = V \\Lambda V^\\top$: $(e^A)_{ii} = \\sum_k V_{ik}^2 e^{\\lambda_k}$ and likewise with\n$\\cosh$, in $O(n^3)$ time. Matches NetworkX's `bipartite.spectral_bipartivity` (which\nuses `scipy.linalg.expm`).\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~is_bipartite`) \n\n:   Check whether the graph is exactly bipartite.\n\n[](`~estrada_index`) \n\n:   The sum over all closed walks, of odd and even length.\n\n[](`~subgraph_centrality`) \n\n:   The closed walks that start and end at each node.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA square has only even cycles and scores `1`, while a triangle's odd cycle brings its\nscore down:\n\n::: {#3659d6e5 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nsquare = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\"), (\"D\", \"A\")]\n)\ntriangle = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"A\")])\n\nsquare.spectral_bipartivity(), round(triangle.spectral_bipartivity(), 3)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(1.0, 0.843)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Almost bipartite\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network, each station placed at its `pos` on the map.\nIt isn't bipartite, but it's close: its only triangles are the two that share the track\nfrom Central to Riverside, and the stations on them score lowest:\n\n::: {#f85d45ff .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\nbipartivity = metro.spectral_bipartivity(nodes=metro.get_node_ids())\nranked = sorted(bipartivity, key=bipartivity.get)\nlabel = metro.get_label_from_id\n\n(\n    round(metro.spectral_bipartivity(), 3),\n    [(label(n), round(bipartivity[n], 3)) for n in ranked[:4]],\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(0.976,\n [('Central', 0.583),\n  ('Riverside', 0.663),\n  ('Old Town', 0.737),\n  ('Market', 0.78)])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#2048c7b1 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro.set_node_attrs(\"bipartivity\", bipartivity).plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"bipartivity\", color_scale=\"sequential\",\n    label_by=\"label\",\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-bedcb8ea:#6e9cd5;--ect-ce3c29cd:#5884bc;--ect-97f76ec5:#254e84;--ect-af0f490b:#163e74;--ect-8133927f:#416ca3;--ect-826951ff:#0e376c;--ect-8eff6c8a:#406ba2;--ect-975840b8:#86b6ef;--ect-6425850a:#0d366b;--ect-7bcf0c07:#3f69a1;--ect-4a608c77:#2f5990;--ect-e28c6970:#194278;--ect-db3f8f40:#4c77af;--ect-e58b2c1a:#113a6f;--ect-f8094ac6:#79a8e1;--ect-472663e1:#6d9bd3;--ect-6826a5f9:#608ec6;--ect-9d43aea2:#5480b8;--ect-5ee57d66:#4874ab;--ect-3c980f0e:#3c679e;--ect-ec386ef0:#305a91;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-41288e7c:#4d6d95;--ect-ac3f80c3:#3d5c83;--ect-b03e49fa:#19365c;--ect-0ed25f94:#0f2b51;--ect-3838da4c:#2d4b72;--ect-67c7df97:#09264b;--ect-7b967146:#2c4a71;--ect-6970a796:#5d7fa7;--ect-bf50105f:#09254a;--ect-65593a52:#2c4970;--ect-9e444a17:#203e64;--ect-cc719475:#112e54;--ect-bbffd9a2:#35537a;--ect-abcb2494:#0b284d;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-bedcb8ea:#3c6aa9;--ect-ce3c29cd:#5b84bb;--ect-97f76ec5:#a8c4e7;--ect-af0f490b:#c0d7f4;--ect-81